to communicate this pleasant news. to enter into conflict and were resolved upon bringing about Rāma's wellbeing.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-61-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5059006","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"826bef02e7afcbb285fb7c9eca2ef4d45fad4646e219fd4ed8d5c3209c222b18","compact":"2043ebf15dee90d8fd28649cd40702300a16310f76103d5f2af265a74eaa202a","nasal":"9af2b9fb852e20ecb46d6b7e0e8a08f81e1ea795324ef6044a270d0d25328603"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-59-7","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":59,"verse":7,"english":"And leaping and ascending the sky they got at the Madhuvana, (An orchard teeming with various trees bearing delicious and sweet fruits) preserved by Sugrīva, resembling the celestial garden, covered with many trees, picturesque and incapable of being divastated by any.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.7,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-61-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5059007","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5c8e98d49a97f10960c7c80328f19cfe8117e6d8577961e53d33bef60fe4952d","compact":"064827c941fb8622d5a70aaf5d77fdf2cc2c44b0b458096fb6bd91bfa9e1b79b","nasal":"7c1b0ef0efa82a9236563364ce0d07769b68adea52be6cabc5173cc25ca7363d"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-59-8","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":59,"verse":8,"english":"And leaping and ascending the sky they got at the Madhuvana, (An orchard teeming with various trees bearing delicious and sweet fruits) preserved by Sugrīva, resembling the celestial garden, covered with many trees, picturesque and incapable of being divastated by any.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-61-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5059008","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","english