,"duttRefs":["DUTT-5-61-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5059011","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9511f74f8820fefae4cc41d451ad644077748e70fc76dbe833275604485c011b","compact":"03d8b34020ae77115e844587c853ffc87f15bce6d3a98257464081d4d7f322cd","nasal":"a703584dd2bb864cf6a81d621de254745e5031efb01ab90247627bf359bdc37d"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-59-12","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":59,"verse":12,"english":"And being thus commanded by the intelligent prince-Vāli's son, those monkeys ascended the trees infested with bees and feasting on fragrant fruit and roots, were greatly delighter and intoxicated.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.884,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-61-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5059012","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0bdcb081421eb45e74ef2272a7e1bd688a0a45fa7a2e6a8af078ed00a7920349","compact":"e89c7d8f02a2dada3e9937799e62b629aa0c53e23ea5310955208ca047eb213d","nasal":"b5ceffdea00351dfe8fbc96a131896fc2afc1e743daa0a590ee69fd041f16093"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-59-13","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":59,"verse":13,"english":"And thereupon those monkeys, beside themselves with joy for being allowed to drink honey began to dance hither and thither.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.823,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-61-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5059013","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"37b4fbb0452fffaf3e7b46239e34b585f74c6fe61c17742c953a3700abbdf88a","compact":"154cd2df6ba5ef09200798a64e1051e19e7accd18a5418a0126047887b38ebe9","nasal":"7590e92a9257ce0bdd03a744a5f7619c2b1da1dd87ab06e5826d74a367299715"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-59-14","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":59,"verse":14,"english":"Some sang, some laughed, some danced, some bowed down, some read, some walked hither, some leaped and some talked at random.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.679,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-61-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5059014","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a1e7a5c1317707749d4675da2551b728a794be06c8a572be8cd5483a8a15bb6d","compact":"1a641776bc62fd5dea3319569959b3692e2c1181956d094f7947f133fcb52af6","nasal":"6e8a6804c4eeefa849a1ff6df81668ecf9b98070c059704557914d0abcf2a184"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-59-15","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":59,"verse":15,"english":"Some sprang upon one one another, some quarrelled with one another, some leaped from one tree to another, and some jumped down on the earth from the tops of the trees.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.505,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-61-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5059015","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d017a5225c1bab26567260894d2088ad445d1226dbb04aa8d45bc58a92c24e00","compact":"ceecd0c76e6b646a5ae0b5d0b7988dca4acc424c709b376ed3e30f9d45c0b139","nasal":"c687dbc84f7b693d2d157d60e8155f47c965425f962400e6859ec946b5c88961"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-59-16","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":59,"verse":16,"english":"Some rose up with great velocity from the earth to the tops of the huge trees-some sang, other approached them laughing—some wept and others approached them weeping.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.742,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-61-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5059016","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2520b286c246d4ae921a7fe017351195db8bbfe14b6fef450feefc575172c1f8","compact":"3dd73b95d4ba26fe6c961b7864041836eca91306ea190cc85ef91241c6649aab","nasal":"b3ceda37e91f46c0ed5471945918d81d0dbf05ce2b36e41e9a398af4218ad516"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-59-17","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":59,"verse":17,"english":"Some were stricking with their nails and others struck them in return. And thus the entire monkey host were bewildered with intoxication. There was none among them who was not drunk and none who was not excited with pride.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.525,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-61-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5059017","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c217e56d4d051671f6ec6dda9cd9acc818a59e55bc3af9c139b801ef4fe8e93c","compact":"696356cf75c3ff58ced71e6daf90c92a0c4816b37a62dba72cf7332dd8576d8c","nasal":"9e46d77e72d765686c7eae8fa557ba5ad2ab95bc2d8b83ee7b32be241e2bbc13"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-59-18","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":59,"verse":18,"english":"Thereupon beholding all the fruits eaten up and the trees divested of leaves and flowers, the monkey Dadhimukha and worked up with ire and attempted to prevent them.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.835,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-61-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5059018","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"092e67435d0585edcf5ab031f59a652c921db2f29666480f68594a5828d695fc","compact":"1c71f456e8e92a1eb93c33257a905f5d3ef68e723531843eb9aa7e1672360af0","nasal":"1c71f456e8e92a1eb93c33257a905f5d3ef68e723531843eb9aa7e1672360af0"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-59-19","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":59,"verse":19,"english":"And that heroic, elderly monkey, the guard of the garden, was in return remonstrated with by them who were greatly intoxicated. Thereat the highly spirited monkey again made up his mind to protect the garden from their devastations.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.689,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-61-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5059019","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5988cab33dd1821c1c1662f1620583bb7dae03277f9dd238b33c98e9d3124511","compact":"36dbd2a3379c3104fdd1c28351131d5cd8a8335f36bf58cee7ba6c4c37dad57e","nasal":"36dbd2a3379c3104fdd1c28351131d5cd8a8335f36bf58cee7ba6c4c37dad57e"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-59-20","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":59,"verse":20,"english":"He used harsh words, undauntedly towards some, struck the weak with his palm, quarrelled with some, and consoled others with soothing words.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.621,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-61-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5059020","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d00440ddb20bab5c90140183fcacbd6771b6adf5444d59530a7d4d5d8abf68dd","compact":"2de24df2a41d5954549306a5b65c7c4a2465faedb535d0350c127ea9713caafd","nasal":"2de24df2a41d5954549306a5b65c7c4a2465faedb535d0350c127ea9713caafd"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-59-21","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":59,"verse":21,"english":"They were greatly excited with drink, and being prevented forcibly by Dadhimukha, they giving up all fear, began to pull him.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.535,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-61-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5059021","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8ffa874f9ad64b75deed80d46bf5c9a161b1dea454bc0ac06bc6acb67510317a","compact":"19f54b01c1c0c8d97ef80754e82dc0c33df62b9c9797746c3461cde15bead5d2","nasal":"19f54b01c1c0c8d97ef80754e82dc0c33df62b9c9797746c3461cde15bead5d2"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-59-22","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":59,"verse":22,"english":"And striking him with their nails, biting him with teeth, crushing him with their palms and feel, they being drunk, almost reduced him to death and devastated the mangoe forest.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.314,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-61-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5059022","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6b64b8df14b445d19e31c60a7b05666ad5617e7b8990b5c79a8294708aab3095","compact":"cee8b112ce130a3dc4616ea6cb3ede2cb0b5561c198bf409fcf389da5b1dd673","nasal":"ab92fea5a9143727b68c34265c740febef5128549666f96570627dc27d840f9b"}}]
